y throughout the Modern era. Established during a time of significant transformation in American society, The Atlantic emerged against the backdrop of the Civil War and the burgeoning industrial age, positioning itself as a platform for influential writers including Ralph Waldo Emerson, Mark Twain, and later, figures such as James Baldwin and Ta-Nehisi Coates. Its commitment to exploring the complexities of American life and politics has rendered it a significant institution in the landscape of American journalism and thought.

